  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[2,5]$ and $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[2,5]$ are $2$ and $5.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are $0,1,3,$ and $4.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $(6,10]$ has a boundary point $6$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
